From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:08:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix vfio const class register write fault on pre-const
 kernels

Pre-6.4 kernels implement class_register(struct class *) by writing
into the struct during registration (e.g. cls->p = subsys_private and
cls->dev_kobj = sysfs_dev_char_kobj).
The upstream "static const struct class" definitions land in read-only .rodata,
so those stores fault at vfio module init:

Call trace:
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BUG: unable to handle page fault for address: ffffffffc0f556c0
PGD 5fe014067 P4D 5fe014067 PUD 5fe016067 PMD 102366067 PTE 800000010639a161
RIP: 0010:__class_register+0x16f/0x180
Call Trace:
 <TASK>
 vfio_group_init+0x6d/0xa8 [vfio]
 ? 0xffffffffc0cb1000
 __init_backport+0x29/0x76 [vfio]
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Drop the const qualifier from vfio_class and vfio_device_class when
BPM_CLASS_DEVNODE_CONST_NOT_PRESENT is set, so the objects live in
writable memory on those kernels.

Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
---
 drivers/vfio/group.c     | 4 ++++
 drivers/vfio/vfio_main.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/vfio/group.c b/drivers/vfio/group.c
index 51f4d0e..7607c93 100644
--- a/drivers/vfio/group.c
+++ b/drivers/vfio/group.c
@@ -20,7 +20,11 @@ static char *vfio_devnode(struct device *dev, umode_t *mode);
 #else
 static char *vfio_devnode(const struct device *, umode_t *);
 #endif
+#ifdef BPM_CLASS_DEVNODE_CONST_NOT_PRESENT
+static struct class vfio_class = {
+#else
 static const struct class vfio_class = {
+#endif
 	.name	= "vfio",
 	.devnode = vfio_devnode
 };
diff --git a/drivers/vfio/vfio_main.c b/drivers/vfio/vfio_main.c
index 612eb6f..1f51152 100644
--- a/drivers/vfio/vfio_main.c
+++ b/drivers/vfio/vfio_main.c
@@ -72,7 +72,11 @@ static char *vfio_device_devnode(const struct device *dev, umode_t *mode)
 	return kasprintf(GFP_KERNEL, "vfio/devices/%s", dev_name(dev));
 }
 
+#ifdef BPM_CLASS_DEVNODE_CONST_NOT_PRESENT
+static struct class vfio_device_class = {
+#else
 static const struct class vfio_device_class = {
+#endif
 	.name		= "vfio-dev",
 	.devnode	= vfio_device_devnode
 };
